.TH SDL_powf 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_powf \- Raise
.BR x
to the power
.BR y

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "float SDL_powf(float x, float y);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Domain:
.BR "-INF <= x <= INF" ,

.BR "-INF <= y <= INF"
.PP
Range:
.BR "-INF <= z <= INF"
.PP
If
.BR y
is the base of the natural logarithm (e), consider using
.BR SDL_exp
instead\[char46]
.PP
This function operates on single-precision floating point values, use
.BR SDL_pow
for double-precision floats\[char46]
.PP
This function may use a different approximation across different versions, platforms and configurations\[char46] i\[char46]e, it can return a different value given the same input on different machines or operating systems, or if SDL is updated\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
the base\[char46]
.TP
.I y
the exponent\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.BR x
raised to the power
.BR y \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

